<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Achieng wants a motorbike that costs Ksh <m>{150\,000}</m> cash.</p><p>Option 1, hire purchase: a deposit of Ksh <m>{30\,000}</m> and <m>{18}</m> monthly instalments of Ksh <m>{8200}</m>.</p><p>Option 2: borrow Ksh <m>{150\,000}</m> from a SACCO at <m>{14}\%</m> per annum simple interest, repaying it all over <m>{18}</m> months.</p><p>(a) Find the total cost of option 1.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) Find the total repaid to the SACCO.</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans2"/>  </p><p>(c) Which option costs less? [ Hire purchase | The SACCO loan ]  </p><p>(d) By how much?</p><p>Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ans4"/>  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Hire purchase: <m>{30\,000} + {18} \times {8200} = {30\,000} + {147\,600} = {177\,600}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>{18}</m> months is <m>{1.5}</m> years. Interest <m>= \dfrac{{150\,000} \times {14} \times {1.5}}{100} = {31\,500}</m>, so the SACCO is repaid <m>{150\,000} + {31\,500} = {181\,500}</m>.</p><p>(c) and (d) Hire purchase costs less, by <m>{181\,500} - {177\,600} = {3900}</m>. Paying cash is cheapest of all, if you have the money.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>177600</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>181500</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p>Hire purchase</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>3900</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>